Practice by recounting your day: 'Mangwanani ndakamuka na6, ndakadya, ndakaenda kubasa.' (In the morning I woke at 6, ate, went to work.) Then expand to a full story about a trip or event. Record yourself and check verb tenses. Common mistakes: mixing up '-aka-' and '-a-'âuse '-aka-' for specific past actions.

This lesson enables you to share experiences, from village tales to business reports. In African oral tradition, storytelling is central; mastering past tense makes your narratives vivid and credible. Practice with elders or friends, and listen to Shona radio dramas for natural usage.
